/** \page release_notes Revision History

\section rev_3_6_16 Revision 3.6.16 [Unreleased]

- Functional changes.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
   - Typos and unhelpful information in status messages.
- Performance changes.
- Bug fixes.
  - When starting another app in Windows, the batch script window is not closed.
  - Occasional exception when closing ZZALOG: probable race hazard while closing ticker.

\section rev_3_6_15 Revision 3.6.15

- Functional changes.
  - Add feature to configure the font in which status messages are displayed.
  - Restore original FlLog emulation (removed in 3.6.12) after bug fixes therewith.
  - Add QTH in QSO record as source of location data, looking up in openweather.org.
  - Add mirroring of logbook file to support use of network files.
  - Cold start: require minimum amount of user data.
  - Add feature to power the rigs down.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Prevent banner from always appearing on top of dashboard.
  - Remove cursor manipulation.
  - Allow terminal-style monospace font for log tables.
  - Change presentation in qso_dxcc pane: describe source of latitude and longitude more clearly.
  - Add LGPL licence.
  - Separate API documentation for ZZALOG and ZZACOMMON.
- Performance changes.
  - None.
- Bug fixes.
  - Improve resilience to FlRig status when launching ZZALOG
  with auto-start feature enabled. 
  - Country data file timestamps not recorded correctly.
  - Spurious updates to QSO records with non-critical data.
  - Callsign decode partly left displayed when QSO not selected.
  - Correct or remove misleading messages.

\section older Older revisions

\subsection rev_3-6-14 Revision 3.6.14

- Functional changes.
  - Added country data viewer as part of main window.
  - Added switch -o (-off-air) to inhibit trying to start rigs automatically.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes. 
  - Use lighter colours in banner.
  - Display count-up while waiting to connect rig.
- Performance changes.
  - None.
- Bug fixes.
  - Incorrect callsign parsing when time-validity of two allocations start and
  end at the same date and time.
  - Gibberish displayed when reporting rig connection timing issues.
  - Incorrectly sets MY_RIG to previous QSO value instead of picking current rig.
  - Needed to escape non-alphanumeric characters when uploading to QRZ.com.
  - Issues reading country data.
  - Cold start issue: default location needs a city or locator.

Tested with hamlib release 4.7.0.

\subsection rev_3-6-13 Revision 3.6.13

- Functional changes.
  - Added iso.csv: ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country codes and names for locating
  QTH information.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Standardising app identification across ZZACOMMON apps.
  - Change names and namespaces for ZZACOMMON classes and stand-alone methods.
  - Move QSL configuration file to standard location, and only prompt for
  QSL Cards directory when needed.
  - Move non-user API keys to keys.json. 
  - Move installation directory for reference data to allow user-only installation.
- Perfomance changes.
  - ZZALOG used 200% CPU when idling. 
- Bug fixes.
  - Logged frequency and start time not being set correctly from FlDigi.
  - Problems with cold-start with minimal user input during configuration.
    - Exception from WX handler with no user location.
    - Open user station dialog before any other dialog.
    - Force user to supply location and name during configuration.
  - False error when reading "No QSL" list.

\subsection rev_3-6-12 Revision 3.6.12

- Functional changes
  - Close banner now closes the application.
  - Add keyboard shortcuts for critical buttons in \ref qso_manager.
  - Add CTRL-s (Save) and CTRL-x (Exit) in script file viewer.
  - Download files from www.country-files.com within ZZALOG.
  - Add check on Hamlib rig number versus model name.
  - Replace FLLog emulation with listening for UDP packets from FlDigi.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Code linting - resulted in some performnace improvement.
  - Create separate repository for code that can be reused in other projects (ZZACOMMON).
  - Add timestamp to banner status messages.
  - Make current dirty QSO records a debug option: -d m
  - Make socket diagnostics a debug option: -d k
  - Remember previous banner size and restore it.
- Perfomance changes.
  - Use system command to copy log to backup file.
- Bug fixes:
  - Progress dial not showing load cty.json progress correctly.
  - Improved focus handling in QSO entry dialog.
  - Settings get corrupted when updating twice in same scope.
  - Misreads exception VERSION in country-data.com cty.csv file.
  - Exception when trying to delete a single entry from an active net.
  - No way to specify where to find ALL.TXT file used by WSJT-X.
  - Switch "-t" ignored when saving a net.

\subsection rev_3-6-11 Revision 3.6.11

- Revision 3.6.10 unnecessarily renamed executable:
reverting to zzalog.
- Move contest specific sources to separate library.

\subsection rev_3-6-10 Revision 3.6.10 [Deprecated]

- Added multicast support for UDP in Windows. (Already present for Linux).
- Changed build system to CMake on Windows and Linux.
- Cosmetic changes.
  - Current QSO frequency does not show up properly in LIGHT mode.
- Bug fixes:
  - "Don't QSL" list ignored when saving a net.
  - Adding an application should select the new tab in qso_apps.
  - apps.json doesn't load correctly if no script defined for app.
  - Remove use of "using namespace std;" per modern coding guidelines.

\subsection rev_369 Revision 3.6.9

- Redesigned station dialog and initialisation of station data.
- Add ability to edit band plan data.
- Move qso_apps configuration data to separate JSON file.
- Reinstate club operator log-in.
- Better handling of configuration data between development and release versions. 
Features to assist cold- and warm-start testing.
- Add feature to allow a list of "Don't QSL" callsigns.
- Cosmetic changes.
- Performance improvements.
  - Reduce look-ups while loading ADIF file.
  - Save country data as single file between updates.
- Bug fixes:
  - Wrong include file.
  - Reflect changes in station dialog to station fields in dashboard.
  - Revise Google Maps location algorithm.

\subsection rev_368A Revision 3.6.8A

- Further issues with "luke-warm" start.

\subsection rev_368 Revision 3.6.8

- Testing proposal to ignore unpaired '<' in reading ADI format.
- Removed special behaviour for club stations.
- Added PDF version of userguide.
- Used pugixml as XML engine.
- Added panel with solar data.
- Cosmetic changes.
- Bug fixes:
  - Changing the displayed fields does not get saved.
  - Falsely claims data has been edited when closing ZZALOG.
  - ADX parsing not returning correct response (OK/error).
  - JSON ADIF Band enumeration is lower-case.
  - Errors with cold-start.
  - Focus management in QSO entry broken when added userguide.

\subsection rev_367 Revision 3.6.7

- Save a copy of the latest data before each save. Upto 8 copies are saved.
- Add further acknowledgments of third-party data and libraries.
- Refinements to callsign parsing algorithm.
- Add Doxygen comments to all header files. This identified a number
of redundancies in the code that have been removed.
- Move eQSL image download progress display to main progress dial.
- Migrate configuration files and WX download from XML to JSON.
- Include ADIF 3.1.6.
- Include hamlib v4.6.5 in Windows build.
- Cosmetic changes.
- Bug fixes:
  - Errors in callsign parsing algorithm.
  - Starting to log QSO in WSJT-X state RX.TX1 results in confusion (revoking previous mod).
  - Code check uncovered bug in base contest algorithm code.
  - Displayed clock can be a noticeable fraction of a second out.
  - If there are no QSLs to upload an empty extract is displayed which cannot be cleared from qso_qsl.
  - Occasionally not all records marked clean after eQSL download
   completes and writes data back to filestore.
  - Exception adding an image to a QSL design.
  - Timezone label on clock doesn't redraw properly.
  - Removed "using namespace " per modern coding guidelines.
  - Address performance issues in sorting extracted data.

\subsection rev_366 Revision 3.6.6

- Combine WX tab with Clock tab.
- Change Clock tab to a single tab, switchable between UTC and local time.
- Add "CLOSING" across progress banner.
- Cosmetic changes.
- Bug fixes:
  - Exception when pasting data.
  - Uploads to eQSL.cc cannot be enabled.
  - Some input widgets not getting keyboard focus.
  - Wrong call presented in queries.

\subsection rev_365 Revision 3.6.5

- First documented release.

*/